{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## THE NOT-RESOLVABLE VERDICT NEEDS REVISITING — the two forms behave DIFFERENTLY\n\nRun **30863672922** executed both falsifiers this ticket recorded. Neither clears the parent, so the\nCONCLUSION stands — but the REASONING that produced it was wrong, which matters for the fix space.\n\n    {\"fields\":{\"parent\":null}}                 -> 400 \"data was not an object\"                [req-0055]\n    {\"update\":{\"parent\":[{\"set\":null}]}}       -> 400 \"Field 'parent' cannot be set.\n                                                       It is not on the appropriate screen,\n                                                       or unknown.\"                            [req-0057]\n    sub-task editmeta: NO 'parent' field at all (no declared operations)                       [req-0054]\n\nThe earlier verdict rested on \"the deserializer requires an object, and the update-verb form would\npass the identical value through it\". **That was inference, and it is falsified** — the two forms\nproduce materially different errors, so they do NOT go through the same validation path. The\nupdate-verb form fails as *not on the screen / unknown*, which is a SCREEN-CONFIGURATION shape, not\na type error.\n\nThat is a different fix space than \"intrinsically impossible\". It does not follow that adding\n`parent` to a screen would make it clearable — but it is no longer ruled out by the evidence we had,\nand the honest state is UNKNOWN rather than NOT RESOLVABLE.\n\n**This does not change the operator's decision.** The approved plan — clear a non-sub-task's Epic\nLink instead, and pin that DC still refuses the sub-task case — is already implemented in Gerrit\n1330 and remains the right move regardless: it tests the path production actually takes. Recording\nthis so the verdict is not treated as more settled than the evidence supports."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785803347684795001,"uuid":"c11f1ddf-0459-4a55-9de2-ebf61190b8a9"}